1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,416
Monday morning, Malika's shop exists, but it cannot take a single payment.

2
00:00:04,466 --> 00:00:15,168
In Lesson 16, her checked email created the merchant and made her its first admin, and this lesson is how that merchant earns the right to take money, one checked document at a time.

3
00:00:15,218 --> 00:00:17,040
She opens Documents.

4
00:00:17,090 --> 00:00:23,064
The page says "Company documents", and explains that the bank checks who it works with before switching a merchant on.

5
00:00:23,114 --> 00:00:27,816
Two papers are marked Required: the company charter and the director's passport.

6
00:00:27,866 --> 00:00:31,968
Two more say "If it applies": a licence and a power of attorney.

7
00:00:32,018 --> 00:00:34,248
The bank must know who it does business with.

8
00:00:34,298 --> 00:00:36,120
That is know your business.

9
00:00:36,170 --> 00:00:45,312
A company that signs up in the morning and takes payments by lunch, with nobody having seen its papers, is the one that piles up complaints and disputed payments.

10
00:00:45,362 --> 00:00:48,648
And then nobody can say who it was, or who let it in.

11
00:00:48,698 --> 00:00:53,040
Malika clicks Choose file, picks her charter, and clicks Upload.

12
00:00:53,090 --> 00:00:54,912
The page says "Uploaded.

13
00:00:54,962 --> 00:00:58,920
The bank will review it." The status reads "Waiting for review".

14
00:00:58,970 --> 00:01:01,392
Each file goes into the file store.

15
00:01:01,442 --> 00:01:06,792
The store reads each file's real type from the file's own contents, never from its name.

16
00:01:06,842 --> 00:01:13,032
Someone else tries a trick: a file whose name says it is a document, but whose contents are something else.

17
00:01:13,082 --> 00:01:16,296
The picker lets it through, because it only looks at the name.

18
00:01:16,346 --> 00:01:19,176
The server reads the contents and refuses it.

19
00:01:19,226 --> 00:01:24,432
The store also keeps a checksum: a fingerprint worked out from every byte of the file.

20
00:01:24,482 --> 00:01:31,248
When the file is read back, its fingerprint must still match, so a document swapped after it was checked is caught.

21
00:01:31,298 --> 00:01:34,464
At the bank, Dilnoza opens the admin portal.

22
00:01:34,514 --> 00:01:37,416
She opens Merchants and picks Malika's shop.

23
00:01:37,466 --> 00:01:41,280
Each document has two buttons, Verify and Reject.

24
00:01:41,330 --> 00:01:45,648
Reject asks her to say what is wrong, so the merchant can read it and fix it.

25
00:01:45,698 --> 00:01:47,232
She verifies both.

26
00:01:47,282 --> 00:01:52,608
Only when every required document is verified can the company itself be verified.

27
00:01:52,658 --> 00:01:59,808
If Malika had not confirmed her email, the "Approve documents" button would stay grey, with a message saying so.

28
00:01:59,858 --> 00:02:04,584
Her email is confirmed, so Dilnoza clicks Approve documents.

29
00:02:04,634 --> 00:02:10,032
Then Sign contract, and she types the contract number, as printed on the signed paper.

30
00:02:10,082 --> 00:02:13,872
That number is unique: no two merchants ever share one.

31
00:02:13,922 --> 00:02:15,984
Last, she opens History.

32
00:02:16,034 --> 00:02:19,920
Every move is there: from where, to where, who, and why.

33
00:02:19,970 --> 00:02:21,792
That is the status history.

34
00:02:21,842 --> 00:02:25,728
I think it is the part most teams add last, and it should come first.

35
00:02:25,778 --> 00:02:31,656
It is written in the same step as the move itself, so a move without its record cannot happen.

36
00:02:31,706 --> 00:02:40,584
Months later, when someone asks why this shop was let in, the answer is on one screen: Dilnoza, on Monday, after both papers were verified.

37
00:02:40,634 --> 00:02:45,072
Know your business protects the bank, the card network and every buyer.

38
00:02:45,122 --> 00:02:50,400
The history protects Dilnoza too, because it shows exactly what she saw and when.

39
00:02:50,450 --> 00:02:54,072
Malika's shop now has checked papers and a contract number.

40
00:02:54,122 --> 00:02:55,944
It still cannot take money.

41
00:02:55,994 --> 00:02:58,920
Next: why switching it on needs two people.
